<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs</h2>

<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">(Thm. <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 5.3. ‣ 5.2 Average Certified Radius Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>) Recall that Eq. (<a href="#S5.E7" title="In Lemma 5.2. ‣ 5.1 Probability Lower Bound &amp; Radius Approximation ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) gives us <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\sigma}^{\alpha,n}(p_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\sigma}^{\alpha,n}(p_{A})</annotation></semantics></math> for a particular point with class probability <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})</annotation></semantics></math> is the ideal case with infinite samples (plugging <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S5.E7" title="In Lemma 5.2. ‣ 5.1 Probability Lower Bound &amp; Radius Approximation ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>)). Consider the ratio:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\frac{R_{\sigma}^{\alpha,n}(p_{A})}{R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})}=1-0.135\frac{z_{{\alpha}}}{\sqrt{n}}h(p_{A})\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.135</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\frac{R_{\sigma}^{\alpha,n}(p_{A})}{R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})}=1-0.135\frac{z_{{\alpha}}}{\sqrt{n}}h(p_{A})\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}h(p_{A})=\frac{p_{A}^{-0.365}(1-p_{A})^{1/2}+p_{A}^{1/2}(1-p_{A})^{-0.365}}{p_{A}^{0.135}-(1-p_{A})^{0.135}}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.365</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.365</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>0.135</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0.135</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}h(p_{A})=\frac{p_{A}^{-0.365}(1-p_{A})^{1/2}+p_{A}^{1/2}(1-p_{A})^{-0.365}}{p_{A}^{0.135}-(1-p_{A})^{0.135}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Crucially, <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(p_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(p_{A})</annotation></semantics></math> is almost constant within an interval close to <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, as illustrated in Fig. <a href="#A1.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. For instance, in the interval <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,1)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geq 0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geq 0.7</annotation></semantics></math>, we find <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(p_{A})\approx 12.14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>12.14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(p_{A})\approx 12.14</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting this value inside Eq. (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), we obtain:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{R_{\sigma}^{\alpha,n}(p_{A})}{R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})}\approx 1-1.64\frac{z_{{\alpha}}}{\sqrt{n}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1.64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{R_{\sigma}^{\alpha,n}(p_{A})}{R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})}\approx 1-1.64\frac{z_{{\alpha}}}{\sqrt{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\bar{R}_{\sigma}(\alpha,n)=\int_{0}^{1}R_{\sigma}^{\alpha,n}(p_{A})\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\\
\approx(1-1.64\frac{z_{{\alpha}}}{\sqrt{n}})\int_{\beta}^{1}R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\\
=(1-1.64\frac{z_{{\alpha}}}{\sqrt{n}})\int_{\beta}^{1}R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\\
=(1-1.64\frac{z_{{\alpha}}}{\sqrt{n}})\bar{R}_{\sigma}(0,\infty)\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1.64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1.64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1.64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\bar{R}_{\sigma}(\alpha,n)=\int_{0}^{1}R_{\sigma}^{\alpha,n}(p_{A})\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\\
\approx(1-1.64\frac{z_{{\alpha}}}{\sqrt{n}})\int_{\beta}^{1}R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\\
=(1-1.64\frac{z_{{\alpha}}}{\sqrt{n}})\int_{\beta}^{1}R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\\
=(1-1.64\frac{z_{{\alpha}}}{\sqrt{n}})\bar{R}_{\sigma}(0,\infty)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">In Eq. (<a href="#A1.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), the equality of expanding the integral from <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\beta}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\beta}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> comes from the fact that <math id="A1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(p_{A})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(p_{A})=0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{A}\in[0,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{A}\in[0,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\beta}^{1}R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\beta}^{1}R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly the definition of <math id="A1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{R}_{\sigma}(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{R}_{\sigma}(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the required formula. Interestingly, the derivation holds for density functions <math id="A1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Pr(p_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Pr(p_{A})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\beta,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\beta,1)</annotation></semantics></math> of any form.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">(Cor. <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem4" title="Corollary 5.4. ‣ 5.2 Average Certified Radius Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>) It follows directly from Eq. (<a href="#S5.E9" title="In Theorem 5.3. ‣ 5.2 Average Certified Radius Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) by taking the ratio for <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. For the second item, it follows also from the derivation of Thm. <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 5.3. ‣ 5.2 Average Certified Radius Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>, since the radii quotient <math id="A1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{R_{\sigma}^{\alpha,n}(p_{A})}{R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{R_{\sigma}^{\alpha,n}(p_{A})}{R_{\sigma}^{0,\infty}(p_{A})}</annotation></semantics></math> is almost constant in the interval <math id="A1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\beta,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\beta,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/R_quotient_plot.png" id="A1.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/222;" width="333" height="222" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Plot of <math id="A1.F8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(p_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(p_{A})</annotation></semantics></math> in the interval <math id="A1.F8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.5,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.5,1]</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">(Thm. <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5.5. ‣ 5.3 Certified Accuracy Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a>) Let <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}=\Phi(R_{0}/\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}=\Phi(R_{0}/\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>; then, for <math id="A1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="acc_{R_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">acc_{R_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> we have that:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="acc_{R_{0}}=\int_{p_{0}}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">acc_{R_{0}}=\int_{p_{0}}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Nevertheless, when we use <math id="A1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples, we can measure only the <math id="A1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>-lower bound of <math id="A1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, which, by Thm. <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5.1 Probability Lower Bound &amp; Radius Approximation ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, is approximately equal to <math id="A1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p_{A}}^{CP}=p_{A}-t_{\alpha,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p_{A}}^{CP}=p_{A}-t_{\alpha,n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">So, now a point will be included in the integration if we have <math id="A1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p_{A}}^{CP}\geq p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p_{A}}^{CP}\geq p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Via syntactic rewriting, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\bar{p_{A}}^{CP}\geq p_{0}\Rightarrow p_{A}-t_{\alpha,n}\geq p_{0}\Rightarrow p_{A}\geq p_{0}+t_{\alpha,n}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\bar{p_{A}}^{CP}\geq p_{0}\Rightarrow p_{A}-t_{\alpha,n}\geq p_{0}\Rightarrow p_{A}\geq p_{0}+t_{\alpha,n}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\alpha,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\alpha,n}</annotation></semantics></math> we notice that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}t_{\alpha,n}=z_{\alpha}\sqrt{\frac{p_{A}(1-p_{A})}{n}}\Rightarrow t_{\alpha,n}\leq\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}t_{\alpha,n}=z_{\alpha}\sqrt{\frac{p_{A}(1-p_{A})}{n}}\Rightarrow t_{\alpha,n}\leq\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">since the quantity <math id="A1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{A}(1-p_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{A}(1-p_{A})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{A}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{A}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is maximized for <math id="A1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{A}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{A}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, and has value <math id="A1.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, all points satisfying <math id="A1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{A}\geq p_{0}+\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{A}\geq p_{0}+\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> will be included in the integration, and the interval that will be excluded will be at most <math id="A1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[p_{0},p_{0}+\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[p_{0},p_{0}+\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}]</annotation></semantics></math>. So, we finally obtain:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)\leq\int_{p_{0}}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}-\int_{p_{0}+\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\Rightarrow\\
\Delta acc_{R_{0}}(\alpha,n)\lessapprox\int_{p_{0}}^{p_{0}+\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⪅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)\leq\int_{p_{0}}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}-\int_{p_{0}+\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\Rightarrow\\
\Delta acc_{R_{0}}(\alpha,n)\lessapprox\int_{p_{0}}^{p_{0}+\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now consider <math id="A1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the average value of <math id="A1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)</annotation></semantics></math> on the interval <math id="A1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}\in[0.5,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}\in[0.5,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. By the previous formula, it’s equal to:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\overline{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}\lessapprox\frac{1}{1-0.5}\int_{p_{0}=0.5}^{1}\int_{p_{A}=p_{0}}^{p_{0}+\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}dp_{0}\\
=2\int_{p_{0}=0.5}^{1}\int_{p_{A}=p_{0}}^{p_{0}+\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}dp_{0}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>⪅</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\overline{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}\lessapprox\frac{1}{1-0.5}\int_{p_{0}=0.5}^{1}\int_{p_{A}=p_{0}}^{p_{0}+\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}dp_{0}\\
=2\int_{p_{0}=0.5}^{1}\int_{p_{A}=p_{0}}^{p_{0}+\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}dp_{0}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Fubini’s theorem, we can exchange the order of integration, obtaining:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\overline{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}\lessapprox 2\int_{p_{A}=0.5}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\int_{p_{0}=p_{A}-\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}}^{p_{A}}dp_{0}\iff\\
\overline{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}\lessapprox 2\int_{p_{A}=0.5}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}\iff\\
\overline{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}\lessapprox\frac{z_{\alpha}}{\sqrt{n}}\int_{p_{A}=0.5}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\iff\\
\overline{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}\lessapprox\frac{z_{\alpha}}{\sqrt{n}}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>⪅</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>⪅</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>⪅</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>⪅</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\overline{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}\lessapprox 2\int_{p_{A}=0.5}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\int_{p_{0}=p_{A}-\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}}^{p_{A}}dp_{0}\iff\\
\overline{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}\lessapprox 2\int_{p_{A}=0.5}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}\iff\\
\overline{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}\lessapprox\frac{z_{\alpha}}{\sqrt{n}}\int_{p_{A}=0.5}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\iff\\
\overline{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}\lessapprox\frac{z_{\alpha}}{\sqrt{n}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{p_{0}=p_{A}-\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}}^{p_{A}}dp_{0}=\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{p_{0}=p_{A}-\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}}^{p_{A}}dp_{0}=\frac{z_{\alpha}}{2\sqrt{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{p_{A}=0.5}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{p_{A}=0.5}^{1}\Pr(p_{A})dp_{A}\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math>, as we assume that the mass of <math id="A1.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(p_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(p_{A})</annotation></semantics></math> is negligible for <math id="A1.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{A}\in[0,0.5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{A}\in[0,0.5]</annotation></semantics></math>. This is the required formula.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">(Corol. <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem6" title="Corollary 5.6. ‣ 5.3 Certified Accuracy Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a>) Following the proof of Thm. <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5.5. ‣ 5.3 Certified Accuracy Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a>, put <math id="A1.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}=\frac{z_{\alpha}}{\sqrt{n}}+\text{err}(\alpha,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>err</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}=\frac{z_{\alpha}}{\sqrt{n}}+\text{err}(\alpha,n)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{err}(\alpha,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>err</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{err}(\alpha,n)</annotation></semantics></math> is the error term in Thm. <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5.5. ‣ 5.3 Certified Accuracy Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a>. Plugging <math id="A1.p23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p23.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and subtracting, we get: <math id="A1.p23.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}-\bar{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},N)}=\frac{z_{\alpha}}{\sqrt{n}}-\frac{z_{\alpha}}{\sqrt{N}}+[\text{err}(\alpha,n)-\text{err}(\alpha,N)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>err</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>err</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},n)}-\bar{\Delta acc_{R_{0}}({\alpha},N)}=\frac{z_{\alpha}}{\sqrt{n}}-\frac{z_{\alpha}}{\sqrt{N}}+[\text{err}(\alpha,n)-\text{err}(\alpha,N)]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the proof of Thm. <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5.5. ‣ 5.3 Certified Accuracy Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a> notice that <math id="A1.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{err}(\alpha,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>err</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{err}(\alpha,n)</annotation></semantics></math> is decreasing with <math id="A1.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, making the term in the parentheses negative, from which the conclusion follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Experiments</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Sec. <a href="#S5" title="5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we make the assumption that the distribution <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr[p_{A}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[p_{A}]</annotation></semantics></math> will be concentrated close to <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, and validate this on various image classifiers (Fig. <a href="#A2.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>). Additionally, we plot <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr[p_{A}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[p_{A}]</annotation></semantics></math> for our main VLM and oracle setup (LLaVa 1.6 7b with Gemma 2 9b) as well as for Llama 3.2 11b (using the same oracle), and observe similar behavior; results are shown in Fig. <a href="#A2.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> (in this case, the ground truth class should be "harmless" on all prompts).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F9" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.16088v1/pA_distributions.svg" id="A2.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/318;" width="476" height="318"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>Plots of histograms and density plots of <math id="A2.F9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained for different models and datasets, as shown in the figure titles. The values of <math id="A2.F9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> were estimated empirically using <math id="A2.F9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> samples.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="A2.F9.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center">.</p></div></div>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F10" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F10.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/pA_distribution_VLM.png" id="A2.F10.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/179;" width="238" height="179" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F10.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/pA_distribution_VLM_llama.png" id="A2.F10.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/179;" width="238" height="179" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>Histogram and density plot of <math id="A2.F10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> for the VLM case for the different harmful prompts of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qi et al. (2024)</a></cite>; the values are obtained empirically using <math id="A2.F10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> samples. Left: LLaVa 1.6 7b with Gemma 2 9b oracle. Right: Llama 3.2 11b with Gemma 2 9b oracle. Notice that the probabilities are further shifted towards 1 for the Llama 3.2 case due to its stronger alignment.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Further, we repeat the experiments of Sec. <a href="#S6" title="6 Experiments ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> for different values of <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, e.g <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.25</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=1.00" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.00</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=1.00</annotation></semantics></math>, and study the drop of the average certified radius and accuracy with respect to the number of samples <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Results are shown in Fig. <a href="#A2.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and Fig. <a href="#A2.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> respectively; we find that the theoretical predictions of Sec. <a href="#S5" title="5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> continue to hold also in these cases.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F11" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F11.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/aver_R_decrease_VLM_sigma_025.png" id="A2.F11.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/118;" width="157" height="118" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F11.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/cert_acc_VLM_sigma_025.png" id="A2.F11.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/118;" width="157" height="118" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F11.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/cert_acc_drop_VLM_sigma_025.png" id="A2.F11.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/118;" width="157" height="118" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Evaluation of LLaVa 1.6 with <math id="A2.F11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.25</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A2.F11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.001)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.001)</annotation></semantics></math> over all harmful prompts of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qi et al. (2024)</a></cite>. (a) Average certified radius drop vs Eq. (<a href="#S5.E9" title="In Theorem 5.3. ‣ 5.2 Average Certified Radius Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>). (b) Certified accuracy. (c) Average drop in certified accuracy when using <math id="A2.F11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples instead of the maximum <math id="A2.F11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, along with the conservative estimate of Corol. <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem6" title="Corollary 5.6. ‣ 5.3 Certified Accuracy Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F12" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F12.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/aver_R_decrease_VLM_sigma_100.png" id="A2.F12.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/118;" width="157" height="118" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F12.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/cert_acc_VLM_sigma_100.png" id="A2.F12.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/118;" width="157" height="118" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span></figcaption>
