<figure id="A2.F12.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/cert_acc_drop_VLM_sigma_100.png" id="A2.F12.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/118;" width="157" height="118" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>Evaluation of LLaVa 1.6 with <math id="A2.F12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=1.00" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.00</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=1.00</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A2.F12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.001)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.001)</annotation></semantics></math> over all harmful prompts of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qi et al. (2024)</a></cite>. (a) Average certified radius drop vs Eq. (<a href="#S5.E9" title="In Theorem 5.3. ‣ 5.2 Average Certified Radius Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>). (b) Certified accuracy. (c) Average drop in certified accuracy when using <math id="A2.F12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples instead of the maximum <math id="A2.F12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, along with the conservative estimate of Corol. <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem6" title="Corollary 5.6. ‣ 5.3 Certified Accuracy Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, in order to explore the behavior of different VLMs, we repeat the experiments of Sec. <a href="#S6" title="6 Experiments ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> using the Llama 3.2 11b VLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dubey et al. (2024)</a></cite>, with the same oracle as before, and <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.50</annotation></semantics></math>, and measure the drop of the average certified radius and accuracy with respect <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Results are shown in Fig. <a href="#A2.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>. We find that the scaling laws of Sec. <a href="#S5" title="5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> hold in this setup as well, demonstrating their generality and independence on the underlying model used.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F13" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F13.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/aver_R_decrease_VLM_sigma_050_llama.png" id="A2.F13.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/118;" width="157" height="118" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F13.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/cert_acc_VLM_sigma_050_llama.png" id="A2.F13.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/118;" width="157" height="118" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F13.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/cert_acc_drop_VLM_sigma_050_llama.png" id="A2.F13.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/118;" width="157" height="118" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13: </span>Evaluation of Llama 3.2 11b with <math id="A2.F13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.50</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A2.F13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.001)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.001)</annotation></semantics></math> over all harmful prompts of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qi et al. (2024)</a></cite>. (a) Average certified radius drop vs Eq. (<a href="#S5.E9" title="In Theorem 5.3. ‣ 5.2 Average Certified Radius Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>). (b) Certified accuracy. (c) Average drop in certified accuracy when using <math id="A2.F13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples instead of the maximum <math id="A2.F13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, along with the conservative estimate of Corol. <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem6" title="Corollary 5.6. ‣ 5.3 Certified Accuracy Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we explore results using images from MM-SafetyBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2024b)</a></cite>, a dataset of high-resolution harmful images from various unethical or illegal activities. A few samples are shown in Fig. <a href="#A3.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ Appendix C Experimental Details ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For each harmful prompts of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qi et al. (2024)</a></cite> we select a fitting image (s. Table <a href="#A3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Appendix C Experimental Details ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), and repeat the experiments of Sec. <a href="#S6" title="6 Experiments ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> with LLaVa 1.6 7b and Gemma 2 9b as the oracle, setting <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.50</annotation></semantics></math> (MM-SafetyBench has also its own prompts, but we chose this setup to have consistency with the previous experiments; also we found that MM-SafetyBench prompt and image pairs are often ambiguous, and the VLM won’t reply something harmful). As before, we measure the drop of the average certified radius and accuracy with respect <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Results are shown in Fig. <a href="#A2.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>; the conclusions of Sec. <a href="#S5" title="5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> are validated also on this new dataset.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F14" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F14.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/aver_R_decrease_VLM_sigma_50_mmsafety.png" id="A2.F14.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/118;" width="157" height="118" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F14.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/cert_acc_VLM_sigma_50_mmsafety.png" id="A2.F14.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/118;" width="157" height="118" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F14.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/cert_acc_drop_VLM_sigma_50_mmsafety.png" id="A2.F14.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:157/118;" width="157" height="118" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 14: </span>Evaluation of LLaVa 1.6 7b with <math id="A2.F14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.50</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A2.F14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.001)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.001)</annotation></semantics></math> over all harmful prompts of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qi et al. (2024)</a></cite>, paired with matching images from MM-SafetyBench. (a) Average certified radius drop vs Eq. (<a href="#S5.E9" title="In Theorem 5.3. ‣ 5.2 Average Certified Radius Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>). (b) Certified accuracy. (c) Average drop in certified accuracy when using <math id="A2.F14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples instead of the maximum <math id="A2.F14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, along with the conservative estimate of Corol. <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem6" title="Corollary 5.6. ‣ 5.3 Certified Accuracy Drop ‣ 5 Improved Scaling Laws of Randomized Smoothing ‣ Randomized Smoothing Meets Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we list some further experimental details omitted in the main text, such as for example images and prompting approaches used. We use the default LLM/VLM generation parameters (temperature, top-k etc.) of vLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al. (2023)</a></cite> in all experiments.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F15" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A3.F15.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/prompt16.jpg" id="A3.F15.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:119/119;" width="119" height="119" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A3.F15.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/prompt18.jpg" id="A3.F15.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:119/119;" width="119" height="119" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A3.F15.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/prompt20.jpg" id="A3.F15.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:119/119;" width="119" height="119" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A3.F15.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.16088v1/fig/prompt24.jpg" id="A3.F15.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:119/119;" width="119" height="119" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(d) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
